# Prefer editor-built Godot scenes

Construct scenes with editor nodes whenever possible. Use as few code instancing as possible.

## Do

- Build hierarchy, meshes, lights, cameras, collision, UI, and materials in `.tscn` / `.tres`
- Reference child nodes with `$Path` / `%UniqueName`
- Use `PackedScene.instantiate()` only to spawn reusable packed scenes already authored in the editor
- Keep scripts for behavior, input, state, and wiring — not for building the tree

## Don't

- `Node.new()` + `add_child()` for lights, cameras, floors, walls, UI panels, MeshInstance3D, CollisionShape3D, WorldEnvironment, or materials that can live in the scene
- Rebuild static scene structure in `_ready()`

## Allowed code creation

- Spawning packed scenes at runtime (bullets, enemies, player from `ball_ship.tscn`)
- Truly dynamic one-offs that cannot be known at edit time
